<quiz><question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Finding probability of an event, the intersection of the two and their complements</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p> \(C\) and \(D\) are two events and \(p(D)={@p_d@} \), \(p(C\cap D)={@p_cnd@}\) and \(p(C^C \cap D^C)={@p_complement@}\).</p>
<p>Find the following probability:</p>
<p>(a) \(p(C^C\cap D)=\)[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p>(b) \( p(C)=\)[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]][[feedback:prt2]]</p>
<p>(c) \(p(C \cap D^C)=\)[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]][[feedback:prt3]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked out solution</b></p>

<p> (a) Find \(p(C^C \cap D) \).</p>
<p> We have: \( p(C^C \cap D)=p(D)-p(C \cap D) \).
</p>
<p> \(p(C^C \cap D)={@p_d@}- {@p_cnd@}\).</p>
<p> \(p(C^C \cap D)={@ta1@}\).</p>
<hr>
(b) Find \( p(C)\).<p> Since \(p(C \cup D)=p(C)+p(D)-p(C \cap D)\), then \(p(C)=p(C \cup D)-p(D)+p(C \cap D)\) (*).</p>
<p> We can obtain the value of \(p(C \cup D)\) due to this formula:</p>
<p>\(p(C \cup D)=1-p((C \cup D)^C)=1-p(C^C \cap D^C)\) (#)</p>
<p> When we substitute (#) in (*), we obtain:</p>
<p> \( p(C)= 1-p(C^C \cap D^C))-p(D)+p(C \cap D)\).</p>
<p> \( p(C)= 1-{@p_complement@}-{@p_d@}+{@p_cnd@}\).</p>
<p> Therefore, \( p(C)={@ta2@}\).</p>
<hr>
<p> (c) Find \(p(C \cap D^C)\).</p>
<p> We have: \(p(C \cap D^C)=p(C)-p(C \cap D)\).</p>
<p> So \(p(C \cap D^C)={@ta2@}-{@p_cnd@}\).</p>
<p> Therefore, \(p(C \cap D^C)={@ta3@}\).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
